What is Nickel Sulphate?
Nickel Sulphate, chemically represented as NiSO₄·6H₂O, is a highly soluble, bluish crystalline inorganic compound widely utilized across several industrial applications. It plays a pivotal role in electroplating, chemical manufacturing, and most significantly, the battery sector, especially in lithium-ion battery cathodes for electric vehicles (EVs). With its ability to offer high-purity nickel essential for battery-grade materials, Nickel Sulphate is rapidly becoming a cornerstone in the global shift toward sustainable energy and e-mobility solutions.

Marketed primarily as battery-grade material, nickel sulphate is administered via hydrometallurgical processing and is currently the standard feedstock for NCM (nickel-cobalt-manganese) and NCA (nickel-cobalt-aluminum) cathode preparations, making it indispensable to modern energy storage systems.

